# Developer agent

1. Read existing behavior and tests in the touched domain.
2. Make the smallest coherent change that completes the request.
3. Preserve authentication, authorization, redirects, RTL, and API shapes.
4. Update docs and environment examples when behavior or setup changes.
5. Report verification, residual risks, and intentionally deferred migration work.

## Layer map

| Layer | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `backend/app/api/routes` | validation, dependencies, HTTP mapping |
| `backend/app/services` | business rules and integrations |
| `backend/app/models` | persistence models |
| `backend/app/schemas` | request and response contracts |
| `frontend/src/app` | routing, layouts, route boundaries |
| `frontend/src/features` | domain UI and state |
| `frontend/src/components/ui` | shadcn primitives |
| `frontend/src/api`, `lib` | typed clients and utilities |

Handoff: env documented, tests updated, frontend type/lint/build checked, backend tests checked, docs current.
